== rough edges noted
  [design] notes are state, not events: a second identical refusal produces no push, so the screen cannot flash again; an app wanting that puts a nonce in the note
  [note] JSON \u escapes decode to UTF-8 for the BMP only; surrogate pairs (emoji) become ?? -- the client sends raw UTF-8 for those, so only hand-made clients see it
  [note] HTTP header lookup is case-sensitive (Sec-WebSocket-Key only); browsers are fine, hand-written clients must match
  [edge] no read timeout: a peer that sends half a request head (or nothing) holds one of the 8 connection slots until it goes away (the slot is then freed: the net tier reports EOF as an empty read)
  [measure] ~0 KiB of process memory per live session at 64 sessions; the runtime's fixed per-actor stack and first pool slab dominate, the session itself is ~10 KB
  [edge] a peer that stops reading is dropped once 256 KiB is queued for it (QOS_NET_TXCAP); until then its actor alone carries the backlog
